    "result_text": "The only test class in the project is `AcceptanceTest`, and the full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 2/2 passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a derived, read-only `contactPreference` field to the owner API, following the existing pattern this codebase uses for computed owner attributes (`locality`, `membershipLevel`, `membershipNumber`).\n\nTwo edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `contactPreference` as a read-only `string` enum (`EMAIL` / `PHONE`) on the `Owner` schema, alongside the other derived fields. This makes the generated `OwnerDto` carry the field, and MapStruct maps it automatically.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added `getContactPreference()`, which returns `\"EMAIL\"` when an email is present, otherwise `\"PHONE\"`. It reuses the same \"email present\" check idiom already used in `getMembershipLevel()`.\n\nThe logic lives on the `Owner` domain object as a single-responsibility derived getter (no controller/mapper/service changes needed), consistent with how the app already exposes computed owner fields.",
